A desktop application on the lacodda line's stack: [Tauri 2](https://tauri.app)
around Vite, React, TypeScript, Tailwind and the
[dowel](https://lacodda.github.io/dowel) design system. Scaffolded with
[lyrn](https://github.com/lacodda/lyrn).

## A day in the life

```console
$ pnpm install          # once
$ pnpm tauri dev        # the app, in its own window
$ pnpm lint             # eslint + types + tests, the same gate CI runs
$ pnpm tauri build      # an installer in src-tauri/target/release/bundle
```

`pnpm dev` runs the frontend in a browser, which is faster for pure UI work -
but anything calling into Rust needs the real window.

## Layout

| Path | What lives there |
| --- | --- |
| `src/` | The interface |
| `src-tauri/src/lib.rs` | Where the application starts; `main.rs` is a thin shell |
| `src-tauri/src/commands.rs` | What the webview is allowed to call |
| `src-tauri/capabilities/` | The permissions the window is granted |
| `docs/adr/` | Architecture decisions, newest last |

## The icons

`src-tauri/icons/` is empty until the mark exists. Generate the set with
`pnpm tauri icon path/to/icon.png` (1024×1024 or larger). In the `.ico` the
**largest image must come first**: Windows reads the first entry for the taskbar
and the title bar, and a 16px one there leaves the app looking blurred
everywhere it matters.

